  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The reactivity of compound Z with different halogens under appropriate conditions is given below:<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image5-38b14a60-aac9-4050-a3d6-16e572840d05.jpg\"/><br >\r\n\r\nThe observed pattern of electrophilic substitution can be explained by</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "A6ZDQ",
      "text": "The steric effect of the halogen",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8iyKS",
      "text": "The steric effect of the tert-butyl group",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4FJY",
      "text": "The electronic effect of the phenolic group",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "S0bEZ",
      "text": "The electronic effect of the tert-butyl group",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The reason is the steric hindrance of the tetra-butyl group which is attached to the benzene ring. That is why, the reactivity of compound Z with different halogens under the appropriate condition and electro-negativity of the halogens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>></mo><msub><mi>Br</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>></mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image6-8124a722-bda8-41de-95ff-5a96e3688faa.jpg\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
